.SH "NAME"
neonrelay\-server \- starts the Neon Relay game server
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
\fBneonrelay\-server\fR [\fIOPTION\fR]\&... [\-f \fICONFIG_FILE\fR]\&...
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
The Neon Relay game server is authoritative for gameplay and for every signal that the
reward service accepts\&. It is a standalone derivative of the upstream DDNet server
(see \fIUPSTREAM_BASE\&.md\fR and \fIlicense\&.txt\fR)\&.
.sp
By default the server does \fBnot\fR register with any master server
(\fCsv_register 0\fR, empty \fCsv_register_url\fR) and does not contact third\-party
services\&. Point \fCsv_register_url\fR at your own master server deployment to make a
server public\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\fB\-f\fR \fICONFIGURATION_FILE\fR
.RS 4
Load
\fICONFIGURATION_FILE\fR
instead of the default
\fIautoexec_server\&.cfg\fR\&.
.RE
.sp
All other options are configuration variables, documented in
\fIdata/autoexec_server\&.cfg\fR
and in
\fIsrc/engine/shared/config_variables\&.h\fR\&.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
neonrelay\-server \-f myfile\&.cfg
neonrelay\-server \*(Aqsv_register 0\*(Aq \*(Aqsv_name "Neon Relay server"\*(Aq
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.SH "REWARDS"
.sp
Server\-side reward events are produced by the optional
\fIsrc/neonrelay\fR
module and are disabled unless the server is started with a signing key and a reward
endpoint\&. The module signs match results; it never decides eligibility\&. See
\fIdocs/REWARD_SECURITY\&.md\fR\&.
